1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:05,611
Profit, loss and overhead expenses. Solving single and double transaction problems.

2
00:00:06,233 --> 00:00:09,473
The purchase price is not always the real cost.

3
00:00:09,473 --> 00:00:13,893
A second-hand refrigerator is bought for five thousand rupees.

4
00:00:13,893 --> 00:00:16,523
Then one hundred rupees go on transport, and five

5
00:00:16,523 --> 00:00:20,681
hundred rupees on repairs. So the money actually spent

6
00:00:20,681 --> 00:00:23,973
is five thousand plus one hundred plus five hundred,

7
00:00:23,973 --> 00:00:26,973
that is five thousand six hundred rupees. Sold for

8
00:00:26,973 --> 00:00:30,773
seven thousand rupees, the real profit is seven thousand

9
00:00:30,773 --> 00:00:33,461
minus five thousand six hundred, which is one thousand

10
00:00:33,461 --> 00:00:36,424
four hundred rupees. Not two thousand.

11
00:00:37,093 --> 00:00:39,432
First, decide whether a deal is a profit, a

12
00:00:39,432 --> 00:00:42,528
loss, or neither. Cost price five hundred rupees, selling

13
00:00:42,528 --> 00:00:46,307
price six hundred and fifty: the selling price is

14
00:00:46,307 --> 00:00:49,670
bigger, so this is a profit of six hundred

15
00:00:49,670 --> 00:00:53,176
fifty minus five hundred, that is one hundred and

16
00:00:53,176 --> 00:00:56,122
fifty rupees. Now change the selling price to four

17
00:00:56,122 --> 00:00:58,413
hundred and fifty: this time the cost price is

18
00:00:58,413 --> 00:01:00,369
bigger, so it is a loss of five hundred

19
00:01:00,369 --> 00:01:04,333
minus four hundred fifty, that is fifty rupees. And

20
00:01:04,333 --> 00:01:07,083
when the selling price equals the cost price, there

21
00:01:07,083 --> 00:01:10,213
is neither a profit nor a loss. So there

22
00:01:10,213 --> 00:01:13,028
are two formulas: profit is selling price minus cost

23
00:01:13,028 --> 00:01:15,482
price, and loss is cost price minus selling price.

24
00:01:15,482 --> 00:01:18,264
Always ask which one is bigger before you subtract.

25
00:01:19,087 --> 00:01:21,767
Now the percentage. A profit of one hundred fifty

26
00:01:21,767 --> 00:01:26,147
rupees on a cost price of five hundred rupees

27
00:01:26,147 --> 00:01:29,036
is a profit of thirty percent. The difference is

28
00:01:29,036 --> 00:01:32,055
always measured against the cost price: profit percent is

29
00:01:32,055 --> 00:01:34,507
profit divided by cost price, times one hundred. And

30
00:01:34,507 --> 00:01:37,611
loss percent is loss divided by cost price, times

31
00:01:37,611 --> 00:01:39,863
one hundred. The cost price is the base. A

32
00:01:39,863 --> 00:01:41,887
very common error is to divide by the selling

33
00:01:41,887 --> 00:01:44,338
price instead. That is wrong, and we cross it out.

34
00:01:44,947 --> 00:01:49,034
Let us keep a proper ledger for the refrigerator.

35
00:01:49,034 --> 00:01:52,071
Purchase price five thousand rupees. Add transport, one hundred

36
00:01:52,071 --> 00:01:56,245
rupees, and repairs, five hundred rupees. So the total

37
00:01:56,245 --> 00:01:58,081
cost price is five thousand six hundred rupees. The

38
00:01:58,081 --> 00:02:02,653
selling price is seven thousand rupees, so the profit

39
00:02:02,653 --> 00:02:05,838
is one thousand four hundred rupees. And the profit

40
00:02:05,838 --> 00:02:08,011
percent is one thousand four hundred divided by five

41
00:02:08,011 --> 00:02:12,438
thousand six hundred, times one hundred. That is twenty five percent.

42
00:02:13,287 --> 00:02:16,973
Here is the same idea with a loss. A

43
00:02:16,973 --> 00:02:19,727
flat is bought for four lakh fifty thousand rupees.

44
00:02:19,727 --> 00:02:22,607
Ten thousand rupees are spent on repairs and painting,

45
00:02:22,607 --> 00:02:25,727
so the total cost price is four lakh sixty

46
00:02:25,727 --> 00:02:28,593
thousand rupees. It is sold for four lakh twenty

47
00:02:28,593 --> 00:02:31,457
five thousand five hundred rupees, so the selling price

48
00:02:31,457 --> 00:02:34,107
is smaller. The loss is four lakh sixty thousand

49
00:02:34,107 --> 00:02:36,903
minus four lakh twenty five thousand five hundred, that

50
00:02:36,903 --> 00:02:40,405
is thirty four thousand five hundred rupees. And the

51
00:02:40,405 --> 00:02:43,237
loss percent is thirty four thousand five hundred divided

52
00:02:43,237 --> 00:02:46,753
by four lakh sixty thousand, times one hundred, which

53
00:02:46,753 --> 00:02:48,458
is seven point five percent.

54
00:02:49,127 --> 00:02:50,342
Now a trap. Two tables are each sold for

55
00:02:50,342 --> 00:02:53,112
three thousand rupees. One gives a gain of twenty

56
00:02:53,112 --> 00:02:55,521
percent, and the other gives a loss of twenty

57
00:02:55,521 --> 00:02:58,307
percent. Do the plus twenty and the minus twenty

58
00:02:58,307 --> 00:03:00,067
cancel? It is tempting to say zero percent. But

59
00:03:00,067 --> 00:03:03,407
the percentages act on different cost prices. On the

60
00:03:03,407 --> 00:03:05,270
first table, three thousand rupees is one hundred and

61
00:03:05,270 --> 00:03:07,062
twenty percent of the cost price, so the cost

62
00:03:07,062 --> 00:03:08,872
price is three thousand divided by one point two,

63
00:03:08,872 --> 00:03:10,222
that is two thousand five hundred rupees. On the

64
00:03:10,222 --> 00:03:13,252
second table, three thousand rupees is eighty percent of

65
00:03:13,252 --> 00:03:15,487
the cost price, so the cost price is three

66
00:03:15,487 --> 00:03:17,887
thousand divided by zero point eight, that is three

67
00:03:17,887 --> 00:03:20,738
thousand seven hundred and fifty rupees. The two bases are different.

68
00:03:21,215 --> 00:03:24,184
Now solve the whole transaction. The total cost price

69
00:03:24,184 --> 00:03:26,835
is two thousand five hundred plus three thousand seven

70
00:03:26,835 --> 00:03:31,595
hundred fifty, that is six thousand two hundred and

71
00:03:31,595 --> 00:03:33,702
fifty rupees. The total selling price is three thousand

72
00:03:33,702 --> 00:03:37,102
plus three thousand, that is six thousand rupees. The

73
00:03:37,102 --> 00:03:39,549
selling price is smaller, so overall there is a

74
00:03:39,549 --> 00:03:42,679
loss of two hundred and fifty rupees. And the

75
00:03:42,679 --> 00:03:45,555
loss percent is two hundred and fifty divided by

76
00:03:45,555 --> 00:03:48,955
six thousand two hundred fifty, times one hundred, which

77
00:03:48,955 --> 00:03:52,101
is four percent. So plus twenty percent and minus

78
00:03:52,101 --> 00:03:54,706
twenty percent did not give zero percent here.

79
00:03:55,282 --> 00:03:58,627
Here is the decision process, in five steps. Step

80
00:03:58,627 --> 00:04:02,862
one: find the purchase price. Step two: add every

81
00:04:02,862 --> 00:04:07,617
overhead expense to get the total cost price. Step

82
00:04:07,617 --> 00:04:12,202
three: find the total selling price. Step four: compare

83
00:04:12,202 --> 00:04:14,464
the two. If the selling price is bigger there

84
00:04:14,464 --> 00:04:17,819
is a profit, and if it is smaller there

85
00:04:17,819 --> 00:04:19,135
is a loss. Step five: divide by the cost

86
00:04:19,135 --> 00:04:21,786
price and multiply by one hundred for the percentage.

87
00:04:21,786 --> 00:04:24,051
And when there are several items, compare the sum

88
00:04:24,051 --> 00:04:26,913
of the cost prices with the sum of the selling prices.

89
00:04:27,518 --> 00:04:29,693
One more reminder. Overheads still count when part of

90
00:04:29,693 --> 00:04:31,167
the stock cannot be sold. Bananas are bought for

91
00:04:31,167 --> 00:04:33,898
one thousand two hundred and fifty rupees, and two

92
00:04:33,898 --> 00:04:37,418
hundred and fifty rupees go on transport, so the

93
00:04:37,418 --> 00:04:42,018
total cost price is one thousand five hundred rupees.

94
00:04:42,018 --> 00:04:43,753
Only some dozens are good enough to sell, and

95
00:04:43,753 --> 00:04:46,398
they bring in one thousand five hundred and seventy

96
00:04:46,398 --> 00:04:49,023
five rupees. The spoiled bananas do not vanish from

97
00:04:49,023 --> 00:04:50,907
the cost: the money spent on them is still

98
00:04:50,907 --> 00:04:52,135
part of the cost price. And the profit is

99
00:04:52,135 --> 00:04:56,678
one thousand five hundred seventy five minus one thousand

100
00:04:56,678 --> 00:05:01,129
five hundred, that is seventy five rupees, which is five percent.

101
00:05:01,638 --> 00:05:05,018
Your turn. First: a bicycle is bought for four

102
00:05:05,018 --> 00:05:08,758
thousand rupees, with two hundred rupees for transport and

103
00:05:08,758 --> 00:05:11,886
three hundred rupees for repair. It is sold for

104
00:05:11,886 --> 00:05:14,538
five thousand four hundred rupees. Find the total cost

105
00:05:14,538 --> 00:05:19,278
price, the profit, and the profit percent. Second: two

106
00:05:19,278 --> 00:05:21,723
television sets are each sold for nine thousand nine

107
00:05:21,723 --> 00:05:26,148
hundred rupees. One gives a profit of ten percent,

108
00:05:26,148 --> 00:05:29,107
and the other gives a loss of ten percent.

109
00:05:29,107 --> 00:05:30,969
Did the plus ten and the minus ten cancel?

110
00:05:42,312 --> 00:05:43,564
Let us check. For the bicycle, the overheads are

111
00:05:43,564 --> 00:05:46,072
two hundred plus three hundred, so the total cost

112
00:05:46,072 --> 00:05:48,188
price is four thousand five hundred rupees. The profit

113
00:05:48,188 --> 00:05:50,830
is five thousand four hundred minus four thousand five

114
00:05:50,830 --> 00:05:52,726
hundred, that is nine hundred rupees, and the profit

115
00:05:52,726 --> 00:05:56,444
percent is nine hundred divided by four thousand five

116
00:05:56,444 --> 00:06:01,826
hundred, times one hundred, which is twenty percent. For

117
00:06:01,826 --> 00:06:04,580
the television sets, the first cost price is nine

118
00:06:04,580 --> 00:06:08,792
thousand nine hundred divided by one point one, that

119
00:06:08,792 --> 00:06:10,484
is nine thousand rupees. The second cost price is

120
00:06:10,484 --> 00:06:13,405
nine thousand nine hundred divided by zero point nine,

121
00:06:13,405 --> 00:06:16,685
that is eleven thousand rupees. The total cost price

122
00:06:16,685 --> 00:06:18,602
is twenty thousand rupees and the total selling price

123
00:06:18,602 --> 00:06:20,767
is nineteen thousand eight hundred, so there is a

124
00:06:20,767 --> 00:06:23,952
loss of two hundred rupees, which is one percent.

125
00:06:23,952 --> 00:06:25,883
The plus ten and the minus ten did not cancel.

126
00:06:26,505 --> 00:06:29,165
Let us put it together. First add the overheads

127
00:06:29,165 --> 00:06:31,945
to the purchase price. Then compare the total cost

128
00:06:31,945 --> 00:06:36,065
price with the selling price. Take the percentage on

129
00:06:36,065 --> 00:06:38,601
the cost price, never on the selling price. And

130
00:06:38,601 --> 00:06:42,945
for several items, compare the total cost with the

131
00:06:42,945 --> 00:06:46,000
total selling price. The purchase price alone is never

132
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,278
the real cost. Thank you for watching, and see

133
00:06:47,278 --> 00:06:48,376
you in the next lesson.
